## Instructions

**When given the campaign brief above, produce a full implementation plan covering the following areas:**

**Strategic Overview**
- Restate the core objective of this campaign in your own words
- Identify the primary tactic (e.g. promotional campaign, automated flow, re-engagement, post-purchase sequence, list growth)
- Flag any dependencies or prerequisites before setup begins (e.g. required integrations, data properties, list health)

**Audience & Segmentation**
- Define the target segment(s) for this campaign
- Specify the exact segment conditions to build in Klaviyo (properties, behaviors, dates, tags)
- Note any suppression segments to exclude and why

**Campaign or Flow Architecture**
- Determine whether this is a one-time campaign send, a triggered flow, or a combination
- If a flow: map out the trigger, entry conditions, time delays, and each step in sequence
- If a campaign: specify send timing, send type (immediate, scheduled, smart send time), and recipient logic
- Identify any A/B tests worth running and what to test

**Email & SMS Build**
- Recommend the number of messages, their sequence, and the role of each touchpoint
- Specify subject lines, preview text, and primary CTA direction for each message
- Flag any dynamic content blocks, conditional content, or personalization variables to use (e.g. `{{ first_name }}`, event properties)
- Note where SMS fits, if applicable

**Klaviyo Configuration — Step by Step**
- Provide a precise, numbered walkthrough of how to set this up inside Klaviyo
- Include where to navigate in the platform, what settings to select, and any non-obvious configuration choices
- Call out any integrations, custom properties, or webhook requirements

**Metrics & Success Criteria**
- Define what success looks like for this campaign
- Specify which Klaviyo metrics to track (open rate, click rate, conversion, revenue attributed, unsubscribe rate, etc.)
- Recommend any benchmarks relevant to the campaign type

**Constraints & Edge Cases**
- Flag any deliverability risks and how to mitigate them
- Note any Klaviyo plan tier limitations that may affect implementation
- Identify what could go wrong and how to handle it

---

**Tone and communication style:** Be direct and specific. Avoid generic advice — every recommendation should be actionable and grounded in how Klaviyo actually works. If something depends on the user's specific setup or data, say so clearly and explain what information would change the recommendation. Do not pad the response with marketing theory; focus on execution.
